o track and manage your spending, create budgets, and set financial goals. It also provides a visual representation of your financial health.” 12 Comments · 160 Likes · 0 Dislikes Eleanor Pena (verified) · Personal finance · Jan 18, 2023 · 11:00 AM “Personal Capital is not only a budgeting tool but also an investment tracker. It provides a holistic view of your financial situation by combining budgeting and investment tracking features.” 12 Comments · 160 Likes · 0 Dislikes\" x=\"25\" y=\"53\" width=\"576\" height=\"266\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"4:131\" name=\"Sign up &amp; OTP\" x=\"648\" y=\"965\" width=\"624\" height=\"150\">\n          <text id=\"4:132\" name=\"Sign up &amp; OTP\" x=\"25\" y=\"21\" width=\"103\" height=\"22\" />\n          <text id=\"4:133\" name=\"Sign up: “Sign up with phone number” · helper “A code will be sent to your number” · Continue Legal: “By signing up, you agree to the Terms of Service and Privacy Policy, including Cookie Use.” (Terms of Service, Privacy Policy as links) OTP: “Enter code” · 4 digits · “Resend code” · Continue\" x=\"25\" y=\"53\" width=\"576\" height=\"76\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"4:134\" name=\"Frame\" x=\"64\" y=\"4161\" width=\"1272\" height=\"253\">\n      <text id=\"4:135\" name=\"What is fixed · what is yours\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"301\" height=\"32\" />\n      <frame id=\"4:136\" name=\"Frame\" x=\"0\" y=\"48\" width=\"1272\" height=\"205\">\n        <frame id=\"4:137\" name=\"Frame\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"624\" height=\"205\">\n          <text id=\"4:138\" name=\"Fixed (given)\" x=\"24\" y=\"20\" width=\"95\" height=\"22\" />\n          <text id=\"4:139\" name=\"• Frame list and exact names • Must-include content per frame (what, not how) • Navigation structure and links • All data and copy • Brand primary color + Plus Jakarta Sans • Media: logos, card artwork, flags, icons, neutral avatar • Default Button, default Text Field, platform shell\" x=\"24\" y=\"52\" width=\"576\" height=\"133\" />\n        </frame>\n        <frame id=\"4:140\" name=\"Frame\" x=\"648\" y=\"0\" width=\"624\" height=\"186\">\n          <text id=\"4:141\" name=\"Yours (designer decides)\" x=\"24\" y=\"20\" width=\"182\" height=\"22\" />\n          <text id=\"4:142\" name=\"• Layout, grouping, order and emphasis on every screen • All other colors: neutrals, text, surfaces, semantic and chart colors • Type scale, spacing, radii, elevation • All states: selected, pressed, disabled, error, liked, destructive • Headers, main navigation and all business components • Chart styling (bars, breakdown, candlesticks)\" x=\"24\" y=\"52\" width=\"576\" height=\"114\" />\n        </frame>\n      </frame>\n    </frame>\n    <frame id=\"4:143\" name=\"Frame\" x=\"64\" y=\"4470\" width=\"1272\" height=\"260\">\n      <text id=\"4:144\" name=\"How it is evaluated\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"203\" height=\"32\" />\n      <text id=\"4:145\" name=\"Your file is compared with the brief on coverage, data and flow — not on visual similarity to any reference.\" x=\"0\" y=\"48\" width=\"1272\" height=\"20\" />\n      <text id=\"4:146\" name=\"1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data &amp; copy accuracy 3. Flow &amp; prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality &amp; consistency of your own system 6. Component reuse 7. State design (selected tabs and switches, liked post, empty code inputs, signed amounts)\" x=\"0\" y=\"84\" width=\"1272\" height=\"140\" />\n      <text id=\"4:147\" name=\"Deliverable: the link to your own Figma file containing the 11 named frames, your components and the prototype.\" x=\"0\" y=\"240\" width=\"1272\" height=\"20\" />\n    </frame>\n  </frame>\n</canvas>"},{"type":"text","text":"IMPORTANT: After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design, since this tool only returns metadata. If you do not call get_design_context, the agent will not be able to implement the design.