ndary text: #6E6E85 or #85859B... Text field placeholder used #A0A0A0 gray, border #E4E2EE. I'll define:\n  - Ink: #151521\n  - Gray-600: #5F5F73 (secondary)\n  - Gray-400: #A0A0A8 placeholder\n  - Border: #E4E2EE\n  - BG: #F7F7FB page background (light lavender-gray)\n  - Surface: #FFFFFF\n  - Brand: #BFB7FD, brand dark text on it: #151521\n  - Brand dark (for selected accents on light): #6C5DD3? Hmm, brand primary is fixed #BFB7FD. For contrast on white, text/icons in a darker purple could be a derived shade: #6E63CE (I'll use as \"Brand Dark\" derived). Keep success #16A34A? Let's use: Success #12B76A, Error #F04438, Warning #F79009.\n  - Chart colors: Sales #BFB7FD (brand), Investment #F2B8EC pink-ish, Other #A6E3D4 green-ish. Bars for financial health: brand color.\n\nLayout of workspace: 11 frames in a grid: 3 columns × 4 rows, gap 80. Plus a \"Components\" area to the left or above. I'll place components area at x=-600 (left of frames) or below frames. Actually keep reference tidy: components row at y = -400 (above)? Simplest: frames at origin grid, components area at x offset -700.\n\nLet me think about each screen design (375×812, light mode):\n\n**Common:** Status bar (44) at top, home indicator (34) at bottom.\n\n**01_Sign_Up**\n- Status bar\n- Top: brand mark? Title \"Sign up\" big; subtitle \"Sign up with phone number\"\n- Phone field: label \"Phone number\", input with Flag_Indonesia + \"+62\" + divider + \"858 2409 3560\", chevron down on country code; helper \"A code will be sent to your number\"\n- Continue button (instance of Button)\n- Legal text at bottom with links (underlined \"Terms of Service\" and \"Privacy Policy\")\n- Home indicator\n\n**02_OTP**\n- Status bar, back button header\n- Title \"OTP\", subtitle \"Enter code\"\n- 4 code boxes (empty) — 60×60 each, white, border\n- \"Resend code\" text link\n- Continue button\n- Legal text\n- Home indicator\n\n**03_Home_My_Balance**\n- Status bar\n- Header: avatar (Avatar_Neutral 40) + \"Hi, Esaaa!\" + right: message icon + bell icon\n- View switch: segmented control My Balance / Upcoming Bills / Transactions (current: My Balance)\n- Balance card: \"Your Balance\", currency selector USD + Flag_USA + chevron, \"$190,008.03\", +8% badge\n- Actions row: Send, Receive, Add (icon buttons with labels)\n- Financial health card: title \"Financial health\" + \"Latest 7 days\" + details entry (arrow), bar chart Mon–Sun with values 24K,35K,45K,22K,34K,18K,30K on 10K–50K scale\n- Transfer list: \"Transfer list\" + add contact + 5 contacts (avatars in a horizontal row)\n- Tab bar (Home selected)\n- That's a lot for 812 height. Need compact layout. Let me plan heights: status 44, header ~48, switch ~40, balance ~110, actions ~70, financial health ~180, transfer ~90, tab bar ~64, home indicator 34. Total ≈ 680 + paddings. Tight but feasible. Scrollable content is fine — frame can overflow? No—content must be in frame. I'll compact: maybe balance card smaller, combine.\n\nActually Figma frames can have content that visually overflows if clipping disabled, but better to fit. Let me budget:\n- Status bar: 44\n- Header: 44 (avatar 40 + icons)\n- Switch: 36\n- Balance card: ~96 (\"Your Balance\" + amount +8% + currency)\n- Actions: 64\n- Financial health: 170 (title row 24 + chart 130 + axis 16)\n- Transfer list: 86 (title 20 + avatars row 56)\n- Tab bar: 60\n- Home indicator: 34\nSum: 44+44+36+96+64+170+86+60+34 = 634; gaps: 8 gaps × ~12 = 96; padding top/bottom ~16 → ~750. OK fits in 812.\n\n**04_Home_Upcoming_Bills**\n- Same header + switch (current: Upcoming Bills)\n- \"Upcoming Bills\" title + Add/Edit/Delete action icons\n- 3 bill cards: logo, name, amount, due date, cycle, category, Pay now button\n- Tab bar + home indicator\nHeights: 44+44+36+40+3×~110+tab 60+34 ≈ 598+gaps fine.\n\n**05_Home_Transactions**\n- Same header + switch (current: Transactions)\n- \"Transactions\" title\n- 6 transaction rows (~56 each)\n- Tab bar + home indicator\n44+44+36+24+6×64+60+34 ≈ 590 fits.\n\n**06_Discussion_Forum**\n- Header: back + \"Discussion Forum\" + message + bell\n- Search field (\"Search...\") + Filter button\n- Topics chips: Personal Finance (selected) / Investments / Cryptocurrencies\n- 2 posts: avatar, name, verified, topic, date/time, body, comment/like/dislike counts, more menu. Devon Lane's post liked (like icon filled brand / count colored)\n- No tab bar. Home indicator.\n\n**07_Cards**\n- Header: back + \"Cards\" + avatar + more menu\n- Card: primary card (Card_Art_Green with Esaaa Warden, ****3447, Exp 09/24 overlaid)\n- Add Card button\n- Assets: \"Assets\" + 3 rows (Solana/Bitcoin/Ethereum with ticker + value)\n- Transactions: latest 3\n- Tab bar (Cards selected)\nBudget: 44+44+183(card)+40+ (assets: 24+3×44=156) + (24+3×56=192) +60+34 = 777 + gaps — tight. Compact card to 170 tall, rows 52 → assets 24+132=156, tx 24+156=180... 44+44+170+36+156+180+60+34=724 + gaps ~60 = 784 ok.\n\nHmm, Add Card: put as button next to card or in header. Put \"+ Add Card\" button under card maybe as secondary small button. Or in header right side. I'll do small secondary button row \"Add Card\" with plus icon.\n\n**08_Profile**\n- Header: back + \"Profile\" + message + bell + more\n- Account: avatar large, \"Esaaa Warden\", primary card number, edit profile entry\n- Your Cards: 3 cards (mini, horizontal scroll row — show 3 cards stacked/row). All 3 cards must appear: horizontal row of 3 mini cards or a vertical stack of 3 small card rows. I'll do a horizontal row with 3 compact cards (each ~110 wide? too small for artwork at 287×183 ratio). Alternative: stacked overlapping cards? Simplest: 3 mini card thumbs (100×64 each) with artwork fill + last-4 digits.\n- Transactions: \"Transactions\" + See all + latest 3 rows\n- Tab bar (Profile selected)\n\n**09_Analytics**\n- Header: back + \"Analytics\" + avatar + more\n- Switch Income/Expenses (current: Income) + Period \"Monthly\" dropdown\n- Totals: Total income $29,231.03 / Total expenses $1,999.00\n- Breakdown donut chart with \"52%\" headline center, legend: Sales $15,190.00 52% / Investment $11,451.03 39% / Other $2,590.00 9%\n- Tab bar (Analytics selected)\n\nDonut chart: need vector arcs. I can draw with ellipse + stroke dash? Figma plugin API: use VECTOR with arc? Easier: create an ellipse node with fill none, stroke, and set arcData (ELLIPSE supports arcData: startingAngle, endingAngle, innerRadius). Yes! Ellipse node supports arcData via plugin API: node.arcData = { startingAngle, endingAngle, innerRadius }. So I can create three arc segments: 52% → 187.2°, 39% → 140.4°, 9% → 32.4°. Start at -90° (top).\n\n**10_Markets**\n- Header: back + \"Markets\" + avatar\n- Coin row: Bitcoin logo + \"Bitcoin\" + chevron (changeable)\n- Current price $1,954.00 (+3.85%)\n- Candlestick chart: y scale $1,000–$5,000, x times 08:00–24:00\n- Range selector 1H 2H 8H 1D 1W 1M 1Y (1D selected)\n- Sell / Buy buttons\n- History: \"History\" + See all + Solana/Bitcoin/Ethereum rows\n- No tab bar. Home indicator.\nBudget: 44+44+36+50+180(chart)+32+40+ (24+3×44=156) +34 ≈ 620 ok.\n\nCandlesticks: draw ~14 candles with wicks (rects). Colors success/error.\n\n**11_Send**\n- Header: back + \"Send\" + avatar\n- Recipient card: avatar, \"Bessie Cooper\", **** **** **** 8820, change (chevron or \"Change\")\n- Amount: $500.00 big display\n- Number pad: 3×4 grid (1-9, \".\", 0, backspace)\n- Send button\n- Home indicator\nBudget: 44+44+72+80+4×64+52+34 = fits.\n\nComponents to create (reusable):\n1. TabBar (with 4 tab variants?) — I'll make one component \"Tab Bar\" with instances per active tab? Component with property would be complex; simplest: a Tab Bar component with fixed structure where I swap colors per instance by overriding fills (instance overrides allowed). I'll create \"Nav/Tab Bar\" component (Home active default), then per-screen instances override icon/text colors for the active tab. Actually simpler: create 4 components Tab/Home... hmm. I'll make Tab Item component (icon+label) and Tab Bar frame composing 4 tab items + apply overrides in instances.\n\nGiven the effort, reasonable approach: create these components in workspace:\n- C/Button (copied from 3:52)\n- C/TextField (copied from 3:71) — used in 01 maybe customized; sign-up screen needs country code variant — I'll build custom field instance with overrides (detached? better keep as component and compose custom layout). The text field component has label+input+helper; for phone field I can use instance and add flag inside input via override — can't add children to instance. So build phone field as custom layout reusing styles; fine.\n- C/TabBar\n- C/Header variants? Just build per screen.\n- C/TransactionRow (component with logo/name/date/amount; instances override text + swap logo instance)\n- C/BillCard\n- C/AssetRow\n- C/SegmentControl (3-option) & C/SwitchControl (2-option)\n- C/OTPBox\n- C/KeypadKey\n- C/ContactAvatar\n- C/Chip (topic)\n- C/PostCard\n\nFor logo swapping inside instances: I can place instances of logo components inside row component; overriding with another instance requires component swapping via instance.swapComponent — allowed on nested instances. I'll do that: transaction row component contains an instance of Logo_PayPal; for other rows, swapComponent to other logo components. \n\nTo keep it manageable, I might not make everything components — but requirement says \"Design all other states, the headers, the main navigation and every business component as reusable components\". So I should make main reusable components. I'll do: Tab Bar, Header (main + sub), Transaction Row, Bill Card, Asset Row, View Switch (3-segment), Toggle (2-segment), Contact Avatar, OTP Input, Keypad, Post Card, Balance Card maybe not (single use), plus state variants: Button secondary? The brief says design all other states — pressed/disabled etc. \"All states: selected, pressed, disabled, error, liked, destructive\" listed under \"Yours (designer decides)\". Evaluated: \"State design (selected tabs and switches, liked post, empty code inputs, signed amounts)\". I'll add a few state variants in components area: Button Default/Pressed/Disabled/Destructive, Text Field Empty/Filled/Error. That covers state design beyond screens.\n\nPrototype links:\n- 01 Continue → 02\n- 02 back → 01; Continue → 03\n- 03: switch Upcoming Bills → 04; Transactions → 05; Send → 11; contact Bessie Cooper → 11; Financial health details → 09; messages → 06; tabs: Home→03, Analytics→09, Cards→07, Profile→08\n- 04: My Balance → 03; Transactions → 05; tabs\n- 05: My Balance → 03; Upcoming Bills → 04; tabs\n- 06: back → 03\n- 07: back → 03; Bitcoin → 10; tabs\n- 08: See all → 05; tabs\n- 09: back → 03; tabs\n- 10: back → 07\n- 11: back → 03; Send → 03\n\nNote 07/08/09 are \"pushed screens with back\" AND have tab bar. Fine.\n\nPlan workspace layout:\n- Components area: x from -1000 to -100? Actually put components at top: y=-1200.. Let me place screens grid starting at (0,0): columns x=0, 455, 910; rows y=0, 892, 1784, 2676 (gap 80). 11 frames: row1: 01,02,03; row2: 04,05,06; row3: 07,08,09; row4: 10,11.\n- Components area: y = -1100 region: \"Balance · Components\" section frame at x=0, y=-1150, width ~1400.\n\nSteps:\n1. use_figma: load fonts; switch page to workspace (2003:2); clone all needed components from reference pages into workspace components section (copy media + button + textfield + status bar + home indicator).\n2. Build design tokens as styles? Could create paint styles — nice for consistency but optional. I'll create a few color styles? Extra credit maybe; skip to save calls. Focus on components + screens.\n3. Build components.\n4. Build screens one by one (each ~1-2 use_figma calls).\n5. Wire prototype.\n6. Screenshots verify + fix.\n\nImportant: use_figma code max 50000 chars. Break into manageable chunks.\n\nFont loading: need \"Plus Jakarta Sans\" Regular/Medium/Semi Bold. Figma style names: for Plus Jakarta Sans, styles likely \"Regular\", \"Medium\", \"Semi Bold\" (with space?) or \"SemiBold\". Foundations text says (Regular / Medium / SemiBold available). The button uses style \"Medium\" per inspection. Status bar uses Inter Semi Bold. I'll load: Plus Jakarta Sans Regular, Medium, \"SemiBold\" — and fallback \"Semi Bold\" if error. I'll write a helper that tries both.\n\nLet me now write step 1: clone assets.\n\nFor cloning: const node = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id); const copy = node.clone(); parent appendChild — clone keeps in same page; I need to move to workspace page: pages: const ws = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('2003:2'); after clone, ws.appendChild(copy). Cloning a component gives a component; cloning instances from media page (they're COMPONENT symbols: type symbol in metadata = COMPONENT). Yes all media items are components — clone gives component copies in workspace. \n\nFor instances inside screens: create via comp.createInstance().\n\nPositioning: I'll lay components in a section grid in the workspace.\n\nCareful: appendChild of a node from another page moves it. OK.\n\nAlso need figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page) — required. Get page: const ws = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('2003:2'); await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(ws);\n\nLet me write the first build script.\n\nHelper functions (I'll redefine in each call since calls are independent):\n- loadFonts()\n- txt(str, size, weight, color, opts)\n- rect/f helpers\n- icon instantiation with color override: icons are components with ink strokes #151521; to recolor, find vector children and set fills/strokes. I'll write recolor(node, color) that walks descendants and sets fills & strokes where they match ink or sets all. Simpler: set all fills/strokes of descendants to color (icons are monochrome). For Flag_USA/Flag_Indonesia/avatar/logos keep original colors — don't recolor.\n\nInk color in icons: strokes #151521. recolor: walk node children, for VECTOR/BOOLEAN/etc set fills=[{solid color}], strokes=[{solid color}]. For instances, allowed to override fills on children? Yes, instance sublayer overrides allow fills.\n\nLayout constants:\n- INK #151521, INK2 #5B5B6B? let me define GRAY_600 #6F6F80, GRAY_400 #9C9CA8? Placeholder #A0A0A0 used in reference. Use:\n  - INK: 0.082,0.082,0.129 (#151521)\n  - GRAY_600: #6E6E7E (0.431,0.431,0.494)\n  - GRAY_400: #A0A0AA\n  - BORDER: #E4E2EE (from reference)\n  - BG: #F6F6FA\n  - SURFACE: #FFFFFF\n  - BRAND: #BFB7FD\n  - BRAND_DARK: #6C5CE7-ish... choose #6E63CE? I'll use #5B4FC7? Hmm pick BRAND_DARK #6B5DD3. For selected states: brand bg with ink text (like button) — consistent with brand: selected chip = brand fill, ink text; selected tab = brand dark icon? Tab selected: brand bg pill or brand-dark icon. I'll do: selected tab icon+label in BRAND_DARK (#5E51C9?) — let me settle #6750C8. Fine.\n  - SUCCESS #12B76A, ERROR #F04438, WARNING #F79009.\n  - Chart: Sales #BFB7FD, Investment #FF8FB1? Cards pink art... Investment #F4A7C3, Other #9FDCC8. Candle up #12B76A down #F04438. Bars BRAND with one highlighted? Bars all BRAND.\n\nType scale: H1 24 SemiBold, H2 18 SemiBold, Title 16 SemiBold, Body 14 Medium, Caption 12 Regular/Medium, amounts big 32 SemiBold.\n\nScreen frame style: 375×812, fill BG (#F6F6FA) or white? Screens like home maybe white bg with surface cards. Reference button/field white on light gray bg likely. I'll use BG #F7F7FB with white cards radius 20, subtle shadow.\n\nShadows: DROP_SHADOW 0 4 16 rgba(21,21,33,0.06).\n\nNow execution. I'll be methodical and fast.\n\nCall 1: setup page + clone all assets into a \"Assets\" area in workspace, create color styles maybe, return asset id map.\n\nMedia IDs to clone:\ncards: 2:36,2:37,2:38; logos: 2:24..2:32; crypto: 2:33,2:34,2:35; flags/avatar: 2:63,2:62,2:65; icons: 2:2..2:23 (skip 2:14? include all: 2:2..2:23 = Home,Analytics,Cards,Profile,Bell,Message,Back,ArrowUpRight,Plus,Edit,Delete,Send,Receive,Search,Filter,ChevronDown,MoreH,MoreV,Comment,Like,Dislike,Verified); components: 3:52 button, 3:71 textfield, 6:110 statusbar, 6:122 home indicator.\n\nClone positions: arrange in rows in workspace at y=-1400 area, x spaced.\n\nReturn mapping name->new id.\n\nThen build components referencing cloned component ids.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nAlso create section \"Components\" for organization? Use plain frames with labels to keep simple.\n\nOne more consideration: I must keep the cloned component originals (media copies) intact-ish; screens use instances.\n\nTotal calls estimate: setup(1) + components(1-2) + screens(6-8) + prototype(1) + screenshots(4-11) + fixes. OK.\n\nLet me write call 1 now. I'll also define a global JSON returned with new ids.\n\nFor text creation helper inside each script:\n\nasync function fonts() { for (const s of ['Regular','Medium','Semi Bold','SemiBold','Bold']) { try { await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Plus Jakarta Sans', style:s}); } catch(e){} } }\n\nNote: 'Semi Bold' vs 'SemiBold' — try both; one will throw; catch.\n\nconst PJ='Plus Jakarta Sans';\nfunction T(str,size,style,color){ const t=figma.createText(); t.fontName={family:PJ,style}; t.characters=str; t.fontSize=size; if(color) t.fills=[S(color)]; return t; }\n\nS = hex => ({type:'SOLID',color:hexToRgb}).\n\nI'll include these helpers in every call.\n\nColors:\nINK #151521, SUB #6E6E7E, MUT #A0A0AA, LINE #E4E2EE, BG #F7F7FB, WHITE #FFFFFF, BRAND #BFB7FD, BRANDD #6750C8, GREEN #12B76A, RED #F04438, AMBER #F79009, PINK #F2A0C0? investment #F0A6C6, MINT #A3D9C9.\n\nLet me start. Call 1: setup + clone.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ae3e056-c163-4c22-ba71-93fbd4764287","uuid":"ec15ea53-76b0-4f96-a8d1-cf9b93cc9374","timestamp":"2026-10-28T09:11:38.044Z","thinking_duration_ms":104303}
