access and set fills. That keeps component reuse.\n\nActually to keep prototype links simple, wires attach to top-level frames mostly and specific child nodes (icons etc.) within frames. Reactions can be on any node.\n\nLet me define a helper library in JS that I re-include in each call (since each call is independent). I'll write compact helpers: rect, txt, frame creation, and reference assets by ID via getNodeByIdAsync + createInstance (components) — all my cloned assets are components (they were `<symbol>` = COMPONENT). Card art comps too. Good — I can createInstance for all.\n\nWait: clones of components remain COMPONENT nodes. createInstance() works from any page. Good.\n\nLet me set up the base layout constants:\n- Screen: 375×812, bg #F7F7FB for content screens, white for some.\n- Status bar at top (44pt), home indicator at bottom (34pt).\n\nLet me now write the token + helper foundation and build screens 01 and 02 first.\n\nPlan the screens carefully with positions so each fits 812 height.\n\nLet me write code. I'll use a shared helper preamble in each call:\n\n```js\nconst INK={r:0.082,g:0.082,b:0.129}; // #151521\nconst GRAY={r:0.627,g:0.627,b:0.627}; // #A0A0A0\nconst GRAY2={r:0.45,g:0.45,b:0.51}; // #737383\nconst BG={r:0.969,g:0.969,b:0.984}; // #F7F7FB\nconst WHITE={r:1,g:1,b:1};\nconst PRIMARY={r:0.749,g:0.718,b:0.992}; // #BFB7FD\nconst PRIMARY_DARK={r:0.545,g:0.494,b:0.937}; // #8B7EEF deeper for text-on-white accents\nconst GREEN={r:0.176,g:0.741,b:0.486}; // #2DBD7C\nconst RED={r:0.937,g:0.31,b:0.372}; // #EF4F5F\nconst AMBER={r:0.976,g:0.667,b:0.212}; // #F9AA36\nconst LINE={r:0.894,g:0.886,b:0.933}; // #E4E2EE\n```\n\nHelpers: T(text,size,weight,color,x,y) creates text node with Plus Jakarta Sans. R for rect. inst(id) creates instance.\n\nAssets IDs (cloned):\n- StatusBar 2006:335, HomeIndicator 2006:347\n- Button component 2006:328 (335×52, \"Continue\" text inside, radius 26, primary fill)\n- TextField 2006:330 (335×101)\n- Flags: USA 2006:205