t #4FB7A5? Let me: Sales = #6A5AE0, Investment = #BFB7FD, Other = #F2C14E. \nLayout: donut 160×160 centered at y=250; legend below 3×28. Ends ~560. Tab bar 714. ok.\n\nEllipse arc: node.arcData = {startingAngle, endingAngle, innerRadiusRatio}. For donut segments: Sales 52% → 187.2°, Investment 39% → 140.4°, Other 9% → 32.4°. Start at -90° (top): Sales -90..97.2; Investment 97.2..237.6; Other 237.6..270. innerRadiusRatio 0.7. Ellipse 150×150.\n\n### 10_Markets\n- Header: back, \"Markets\", avatar right. No tab bar.\n- Coin row: Bitcoin logo + \"Bitcoin\" + \"BTC\" + chevron (changeable). y=112.\n- Price: \"Current price\" label, \"$1,954.00\" 28 Bold, \"+3.85%\" green badge. y=150..\n- Range selector: 1H 2H 8H 1D 1W 1M 1Y chips, 1D selected. y=240.\n- Candlestick chart: y scale $1,000–$5,000 (labels 1,000/3,000/5,000 left), x labels 08:00 10:00 12:00 15:00 18:00 21:00 24:00. Candles: ~14 candlesticks with random-ish up/down. Area 327×180. y=290..470.\n- Sell/Buy buttons: two buttons 159×48: Sell (red/outline red), Buy (primary). y=490.\n- History: title + \"See all\", rows Solana/Bitcoin/Ethereum with mini values? Brief: History + See all + SOL/BTC/ETH. Rows with price? Reuse asset values: $12,094.08 etc. Fine.\nBudget: header 56-100; coin 112-152; price 164-224; ranges 240-276; chart 292-472; buttons 488-544; history 560: title 560, rows 588..3×52=744 > 778-34=744 exactly (home indicator 778). OK tight: rows 50 → 738. Good.\n\n### 11_Send\n- Header: back, \"Send\", avatar right.\n- Recipient card: avatar, \"Bessie Cooper\", \"**** **** **** 8820\", \"Change\" button right (option to change recipient). y=112, 327×72.\n- Amount display: \"$500.00\" big centered 32 Bold y=210.\n- Number pad: grid 3×4: 1-9, \".\", 0, backspace. Keys 109×56, rows at y=300.. 4 rows ×64 = 256 → 300-556.\n- Send button 335×52 at y=580? Center bottom: y=600. Home indicator.\n\nHmm wait keypad above button: keypad 290-546, button 570-622. Good.\n\nPrototype links:\n- 01 Continue → 02\n- 02 back → 01; Continue → 03\n- 03: switch Upcoming→04, Transactions→05; Send action → 11; contact Bessie → 11; fin health card → 09; messages → 06; tabs (in TabBar comp)\n- 04: switch My Balance→03, Transactions→05; tabs\n- 05: switch My Balance→03, Upcoming→04; tabs\n- 06: back → 03\n- 07: back → 03; Bitcoin row → 10; tabs\n- 08: See all → 05; tabs\n- 09: back → 03; tabs\n- 10: back → 07\n- 11: back → 03; Send → 03\n\nTab bar comp wiring: Home→03, Analytics→09, Cards→07, Profile→08. Note 03 itself contains tab Home→03 (self) fine.\n\nViewSwitch comp wiring: My Balance→03, Upcoming→04, Transactions→05.\n\nAccountHeader comp wiring: message icon→06. (notifications no target.)\n\nNow components to create:\n1. \"Nav/Tab Bar\" — comp 375×64.\n2. \"Nav/View Switch\" — comp 327×40, 3 segments.\n3. \"Home/Account Header\" — comp 327×44.\n4. Maybe \"UI/Icon Button\" — circle 40 white border with icon; variants differ by icon... create comp with Icon_Plus default? Instances can't swap nested instance easily unless component props. Simpler: build icon buttons inline per screen (they're simple). Component reuse credit mainly from the 3 comps + library comps. Could also make \"Bill Card\" and \"Transaction Row\" components — good for reuse (bills ×3, tx rows used in 05 ×6, 07 ×3, 08 ×3). Transaction row comp: logo instance + name + type + amount + date; overrides: swap logo instance (allowed via instance swap on nested instance), text overrides allowed. Instance swap of nested instances is supported in Figma (swapInstance). I'll make TxRow comp and BillCard comp to demonstrate reuse.\n\nGiven time, plan components:\n- C_TabBar, C_ViewSwitch, C_AccountHeader, C_TxRow, C_BillRow? Bills only used once screen (3 cards) — make comp anyway for reuse of the three.\n\nLet me also think about the button component usage: instances of Button (2006:328) for Continue (01, 02) and Send (11). For 10 Sell/Buy custom buttons.\n\nText overrides on Button instance: instance child text \"Continue\" can be set via inst.findOne(n=>n.type==='TEXT').characters='Send'.\n\nFlags: Flag_USA comp is 24×24, Indonesia 16×16.\n\nAvatar: 48×48 comp; can resize to 40/32? Resizing instance ok if constraints allow; set resize via inst.resize(w,h) — works on instances? Yes resize works but may distort if aspect locked? resize keeps it exact; artwork should scale via constraints. Try resize; if distortion, wrap in circle mask instead. I'll test.\n\nActually for safety, for avatars I'll place Avatar_Neutral instance and resize; check screenshots.\n\nInitials avatars for contacts: circle with initials text (B, D, E, J, C) — brief allows initials.\n\nOK, now write the code. Stage A: create the 3 nav components + TxRow + BillCard components, place in a \"Components\" zone at x=-1700, y=600 area. Then Stage B+ screens.\n\nLet me also create color variables? Not necessary; skip to save effort (evaluation on visuals). Actually \"Define every other color yourself\" — variables aren't required.\n\nLet me write Stage A now. Careful with async font loads before text.\n\nFor the TabBar comp:\n```js\nconst tab = figma.createComponent(); tab.name='Nav / Tab Bar'; tab.resize(375,64); tab.fills=[white]; \n// top border: use a 1px rect at top (LINE color) since strokes on component: strokes=[{LINE}] with strokeAlign OUTSIDE would add outside; use strokeTopWeight? Components support strokeTopWeight if strokeWeight set? Individual stroke weights exist: tab.strokeTopWeight=1; tab.strokes=[solid LINE]; and set strokeAlign INSIDE.\n```\nI'll use individual stroke weights: strokes=LINE, strokeTopWeight=1, others 0.\n\nTab item frames at x=0,93.75,187.5,281.25, w=93.75? Use 93/94 rounding: 93.75 exact works with floats. Icons at x = tabX + 34.875 ≈ 34.9, y=8. Label centered: create text, then set x = tabX + (93.75 - text.width)/2, y=36. Label font 11 Medium.\n\nNames: \"Tab / Home\" etc. for wiring.\n\nIcon recolor helper: walk all descendants incl. the instance root; for nodes with 'strokes' set strokes=[{SOLID color}]; with 'fills' and fills.length set fills. But Bell/Message icons may include fills; setting both fine. Careful: don't recolor Status Bar.\n\nFor inactive gray: GRAY #A0A0A0. Active: DEEP #6A5AE0.\n\nDefault in comp: Home active? Default all inactive; per-screen overrides set active. But overrides inside instance children — allowed for fills/strokes.\n\nViewSwitch comp 327×40: bg #EFEDF7? Light lavender-gray #F0EFF7 radius 20. Three segments 109 each: selected segment = white rounded 18 with slight shadow, text ink SemiBold 12; unselected text gray Medium 12. Default selected: My Balance (index 0). Per screen, need to move the white pill + text colors: make pill separate node \"Pill\" that I move via override (x position override allowed), and text colors override. Simpler: build each segment as frame with its own fill; selected segment frame has white fill+shadow, others transparent. Per screen override: set fills of segment frames. That works (fills overridable). Effects (shadow) overridable too.\n\nSegments: w=109, h=40; inner pill 101×32 at (4,4). I'll make each segment frame contain a rect \"Bg\" and text. Override Bg fills: white vs transparent; effects: shadow vs none.\n\nAccountHeader comp 327×44: avatar instance resized 44 at (0,0); \"Hi, Esaaa!\" at (56,12) 16 SemiBold; message icon button circle 44 at x=239; bell at x=291... 327-44=283 → bell at 283, message at 231. Icon buttons: white circle 44 with border LINE, icon 20 centered.\n\nWire message icon frame → 06 inside comp later.\n\nTxRow comp 327×56: logo bg circle 40 white border at (0,8)? Let's: logo inst 40 at (0,8); merchant name (SemiBold 13) at (52,10); type · date combined line? Brief: \"each with logo, type, date and signed amount\". Merchant name is the logo's brand (PayPal). I'll do name \"PayPal\" (13 SemiBold), sub \"Transferred · Aug 19, 2023\" (11 Regular gray) at (52,30). Amount right-aligned (13 SemiBold) at right, colored. Sign: green for +, ink for −? Use RED for −? Common: green +, ink −. I'll use GREEN for + and INK for −, with − shown as \"-$123.00\".\n\nComp default: PayPal/Transferred/Aug 19, 2023/-$123.00.\n\nAmount right aligned: create text with textAlignHorizontal RIGHT width 100 at x=227,y=12. Also sub-right? Keep single amount.\n\nBillCard comp 327×104: white radius 20, logo 44 at (16,16), name 14 SemiBold at (72,18), meta 11 gray at (72,40): \"Due Sep 05, 2023 · 1 month · Subscriptions\"? That's long; width 200. Then amount \"$21.00\" right top (14 SemiBold) and \"Pay now\" button 72×28 brand bg radius 14 ink 11 SemiBold at right bottom. Layout: amount right-aligned at top (x 279? width 32.. variable). Put amount at (72,62)? Simpler: left col name+meta; right col: amount (right-aligned top), Pay now (bottom right). Meta string \"Due Sep 05, 2023 · 1 month · Subscriptions\" ~ 220px at 11px. From x=72 to x=239 (amount col starts 247). OK.\n\nAmount right: width 64 right-aligned at x=247,y=18. Pay now at x=239,y=56 (72×28).\n\nNow Stage A code. Also create a \"Colors\" documentation? skip.\n\nAfter comps, screens in stages. Let me get going.\n\nOne more thing: reactions inside components — destination frames exist later; I'll add all reactions in the final wiring stage, including comp-internal ones (target comp children by id at that time).\n\nAlso note: cloning Button/TextField/StatusBar/HomeIndicator comps into lib — instances used per screen: statusBarInst = comp.createInstance(); placed at (0,0); home indicator at (0,778).\n\nLet me write Stage A.\n\nPositions for components zone: x=-1700, y=600. TabBar at (-1700,600), ViewSwitch (-1700,680), AccountHeader (-1700,740), TxRow (-1700,800), BillCard (-1700,870).\n\nComponent creation inside page — components created via figma.createComponent() go to current page root; position after.\n\nLet me write the code now. I'll include helper preamble.\n\nImportant: text nodes need explicit font set before characters. Also set textAutoResize default NONE? Default is NONE (fixed)? createText default autoResize='NONE'? Actually default is 'NONE'... I think default textAutoResize is 'NONE' meaning fixed size 100×100 which clips. Safer: set textAutoResize='WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT' for labels.\n\nAlright, code:\n\n```js\nconst C = {\n  ink:{r:0.082,g:0.082,b:0.129}, gray:{r:0.627,g:0.627,b:0.627},\n  bg:{r:0.969,g:0.969,b:0.984}, white:{r:1,g:1,b:1},\n  pri:{r:0.749,g:0.718,b:0.992}, deep:{r:0.416,g:0.353,b:0.878}, // #6A5AE0\n  green:{r:0.176,g:0.741,b:0.486}, red:{r:0.91,g:0.33,b:0.36},\n  amber:{r:0.949,g:0.757,b:0.306}, line:{r:0.894,g:0.886,b:0.933},\n  soft:{r:0.941,g:0.937,b:0.969} // #F0EFF7\n};\nconst S = p => [{type:'SOLID', color:p}];\nasync function fnt(t,w){ const m={400:'Regular',500:'Medium',600:'SemiBold',700:'Bold'}; const wts=[m[w], m[w]==='SemiBold'?'Semi Bold':null].filter(Boolean); for(const s of wts){ try{ await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',style:s}); t.fontName={family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',style:s}; return s;}catch(e){} } }\nasync function T(parent,str,size,w,color,x,y,align){ const t=figma.createText(); await fnt(t,w); t.characters=str; t.fontSize=size; t.fills=S(color); t.textAutoResize='WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT'; parent.appendChild(t); if(align){ t.textAutoResize='NONE'; } t.x=x; t.y=y; return t; }\n```\n\nHmm aligning right requires fixed width; handle separately where needed.\n\nrecolor:\n```js\nfunction paint(node,color){ if('fills' in node && node.fills && node.fills.length && node.type!=='TEXT'){ try{node.fills=S(color);}catch(e){} } if('strokes' in node && node.strokes && node.strokes.length){ try{node.strokes=S(color);}catch(e){} } if('children' in node) node.children.forEach(c=>paint(c,color)); }\n```\nBut this would recolor instance internals — findAll within instance: allowed to set fills/strokes on instance children? Overriding fills of instance sublayers is allowed. Yes.\n\nFor icon instances: `const ic = comp.createInstance();` then paint(ic, color).\n\nWatch out: don't paint avatar/logo instances.\n\nNow write Stage A full code.\n\nAlso make IDs returned for wiring: return map of component ids.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nAdditionally: \"Lib · Source Assets\" frame got auto-layout with all comps — fine, sits at left.\n\nLet me now also double-check PageSwitch: current page is 2003:2 (workspace) — I set it in the previous call, but each use_figma call may reset to... it should persist. I'll re-set at start of each call to be safe.\n\nWriting Stage A code now. Also include StatusBar/HomeIndicator per screen in each screen builder.\n\nFor TabBar labels: 'Home','Analytics','Cards','Profile' fontSize 11 w500.\n\nIcon vertical: icon y=8 (24px), label y=36, h~14 → total 50 within 64, centered-ish. Good.\n\nCode size ok. Go.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ae3e056-c163-4c22-ba71-93fbd4764287","uuid":"ed35ada5-213a-411d-b32f-7ac31decd700","timestamp":"2026-10-28T09:15:17.666Z","thinking_duration_ms":190609}
