{"type":"assistant","message":{"type":"message","model":"kimi-k3","usage":{"input_tokens":88963,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_5_m_tokens":0,"claude_cache_creation_1_h_tokens":0},"role":"assistant","id":"04126ae1c0740a7a032b60b5648d6d7d","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now 09_Analytics. Layout:\n- back (24,56), \"Analytics\" centered, avatar (255), more (307)\n- Switch Income/Expenses (segmented, 327×40 at 116), selected Income\n- Period: \"Monthly\" + chevron — chip right aligned? Put a \"Monthly ▾\" chip next to totals.\n- Donut chart: 200×200 circle with 3 colored arcs (52% deep, 39% pri, 9% amber), center \"52%\" headline. Use ellipse with arcData — figma.createEllipse(), arcData = {startingAngle, endingAngle, innerRatio}. Inner ratio ~0.75 for donut.\n  - Sales 52%: start -90°, sweep 52% → 187.2°; angles in radians.\n  - Investment 39%: 140.4°\n  - Other 9%: 32.4°\n- Totals: Total income $29,231.03 (green), Total expenses $1,999.00 (red) — two rows or side-by-side chips.\n- Breakdown list: Sales $15,190.00 · 52% / Investment $11,451.03 · 39% / Other $2,590.00 · 9% with colored dots.\n- Tab bar active 1.\n\nLayout budget: header 56-100, switch y116 (h40), period chip y168, donut y200-380 (center ~187.5,290, size 160?), totals y400, breakdown y460-600... Let's plan:\n- switch y=116 h40\n- period chip right x=307 y=168 h28 + label? just chip.\n- donut center (187.5, 260) r=80 → y 180-340\n- totals row y=356: two columns\n- breakdown rows y=400, each 44 → 400-532\n- tab bar.\n\nDonut arcs with ellipse arcData: startingAngle measured from 3 o'clock, positive clockwise (in radians). Sales 52% starting at -PI/2 → ending -PI/2 + 0.52*2PI. Investment from there +0.39*2PI, other +0.09*2PI.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ae3e056-c163-4c22-ba71-93fbd4764287","uuid":"16f71121-4e4d-44a8-83c7-573fc7d56d99","timestamp":"2026-10-28T09:29:38.183Z