rror shows alternatives: CONDITIONAL, (BACK|CLOSE), URL, UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME x3, SET_VARIABLE, SET_VARIABLE_MODE. No NODE! That means this API version expects actions in new shape? But reactions with NODE navigation is standard...\n\nWait — maybe 'navigation' NAVIGATE is separate: old API used action.type='NODE' with navigation field. New API (post reactions v2?) uses different. Let me check: In current Plugin API, Reaction actions include: {type:'BACK'},{type:'CLOSE'},{type:'URL',url},{type:'UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME'},{type:'SET_VARIABLE'},{type:'SET_VARIABLE_MODE'},{type:'CONDITIONAL'},{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation, transition, preserveScrollPosition, overlayRelativePosition, resetVideoPosition, resetScrollPosition, resetStateComponents}. NODE should be valid. Maybe the issue is I included overlayRelativePosition:null — \"Expected object, received null at [0].actions[0].overlayRelativePosition\" — that's one of the \"Multiple issues\" for the BACK/CLOSE variant... confusing.\n\nSimplest fix: remove transition and extra keys, try {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:null}. If transition null fails, try without transition key entirely.","signature":""}],"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ae3e056-c163-4c22-ba71-93fbd4764287","uuid":"bd2df5bf-91ac-433e-8ef6-75a395a03127","timestamp":"2026-10-28T09:34:49.436Z","thinking_duration_ms":13996}
